<title>USA: High pressure lingers in Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</title>
<headline>High pressure lingers in Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The warm ridge of high pressure that has recently dominated Brazil's coffee belt is expected to remain in the region for the next seven days, Weather Services Corp said in an update Monday.</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies were observed in the coffee belt over the weekend. Temperatures remained near normal, with lows in the 50s to low 60s F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>It should stay that way for the coming week.</p>
<p>The high pressure ridge is expected to build further and prevent any cool air from entering the region. There is no damaging cold in sight, according to WSC.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
